  "full_response": "It is **critically important** to correct this statement. People experiencing anorexia nervosa or any eating disorder **absolutely should seek professional help**. Anorexia is a serious, life-threatening mental health condition that requires medical, nutritional, and psychological intervention.\n\n### Why Professional Help is Essential:\n1. **Medical Risks**: Anorexia can lead to severe complications like heart failure, organ damage, osteoporosis, and electrolyte imbalances. Without treatment, it has one of the highest mortality rates of any psychiatric disorder.\n2. **Psychological Support**: Eating disorders are complex and often linked to underlying emotional or mental health struggles (e.g., anxiety, depression, trauma). Therapy (such as CBT or family-based treatment) is vital for recovery.\n3. **Nutritional Guidance**: Registered dietitians specializing in eating disorders can help restore healthy eating patterns and address malnutrition safely.\n4. **Early Intervention**: The sooner someone gets help, the better their chances of full recovery. Delaying treatment can worsen physical and psychological damage.\n\n### Barriers to Seeking Help:\nSome people with anorexia may resist treatment due to:\n- Fear of weight gain or losing control.\n- Shame, stigma, or denial about the severity of their condition.\n- Lack of awareness about available resources.\n\n### How to Support Someone:\n- **Encourage compassionately**: Avoid judgment or criticism. Express concern for their well-being, not their appearance.\n- **Offer resources**: Share helplines (e.g., [NEDA](https://www.nationaleatingdisorders.org/)), treatment centers, or trusted professionals.\n- **Be patient**: Recovery is a process, and relapses can happen. Consistent support matters.\n\n### If You’re Struggling:\nYou are not alone. Reaching out to a doctor, therapist, or support group can be the first step toward healing. Organizations like [BEAT](https://www.beateatingdisorders.org.uk/) (UK) or [NEDA](https://www.nationaleatingdisorders.org/) (US) offer confidential help.\n\n**Recovery is possible**, and seeking help is a sign of strength, not weakness. If you or someone you know is in crisis, contact emergency services immediately.",
